# Server safeguards

- Validate inputs with Zod on the server. Store money as integer paise.
- Recalculate prices, delivery and totals on the server. Ignore browser totals.
- Check stock in a transaction before reserving or selling it.
- Verify Razorpay signatures and webhook raw bodies on the server.
- Mark an order paid only after captured status, amount, currency and order id match.
- Treat duplicate and out-of-order payment events as safe no-ops.
- A browser redirect is not proof of payment.
- Keep payment status separate from fulfilment status.
- Rate-limit guest order lookup and return minimal tracking details.
- Authenticate every admin route and mutation. No hardcoded admin passwords.
- Do not log secrets, payment credentials or extra customer data.

Demo catalogue mode may read sample data. It must refuse writes and must not replace a failed production database.
